[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit], :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger], :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-pasteurization-clearance :declare-batch-pasteurized-and-cleared :finalize-food-safety-clearance :declare-batch-fit-for-sale :override-shop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment], :actor/robotics? true, :adr/related ["2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage"], :adr/status :accepted, :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["declare the batch pasteurized and cleared" "declare the batch fit for sale" "clear the batch for sale" "finalize the pasteurization clearance" "finalize the food-safety clearance" "finalize the food safety clearance" "override the shop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override shop safety officer judgment"], :adr/id 2799007513, :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-work-record}}}", :actor/domain :manufacturing/dairy-scheduling-logistics-coordination, :actor/proposal-ops [:log-work-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order], :actor/hard-checks [:maker-verified :shop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion], :registry/maturity :implemented, :actor/isco-08 "7513", :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-safety-concern], :adr/doc_type "adr", :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold], :operation/entry-point :intake, :adr/body "# ADR 2799007513: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7513 Dairy Products Makers dairy-shop scheduling/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7513\n-- Dairy Products Makers** only, Wave3 (production/trades) of the\nrollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete; Wave3 has landed 53 occupations\nacross prior batches as of this session, confirmed via a live\ngit-trees API query of `90-docs/adr/2799*`). This is the first\nfood-processing (ISCO sub-major 75) occupation actor in the rollout --\nno sibling 751x entry exists yet.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7513\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7513\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology` sibling\npresent at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its `:name`\nread exactly \"Dairy Products Makers\" -- confirming the premise, no\nmismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with\n`:required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no\n`:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository existed at\n`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7513` (`gh api` 404 confirmed before\nscaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the\n`7513` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nDairy products makers process milk into cheese, butter, yogurt and\nrelated products -- a food category with real contamination/pathogen\nrisk (e.g. listeria) if hygiene and pasteurization protocols are not\nfollowed. The controlling constraint for this vertical is that the\nclosed op allowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes\na pasteurization-clearance decision or a food-safety-clearance\ndecision (declaring a batch fit for sale), nor override a shop safety\nofficer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor\nis deliberately scoped to DAIRY-SHOP SCHEDULING/LOGISTICS COORDINATION\nONLY -- it never performs cheese/butter/yogurt processing work or\nmakes pasteurization/food-safety-clearance decisions itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, closest\ndomain shape -- a physical-production coordination actor with an\nindependently registered facility and a cost-gated supply-order\nescalation) -- cloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7513` as an OSS dairy-shop\nscheduling/logistics-coordination actor for dairy products makers,\nfollowing the SAME governed-actor architecture as every prior\n`cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Dairy Coordination\nAdvisor ⊣ DairyCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **dairy-shop scheduling/logistics\ncoordination ONLY, never direct processing-execution or\nfood-safety-clearance authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to\nexercise, simulate exercising, or propose exercising a\nprocessing-execution decision, a pasteurization-clearance decision, a\nfood-safety-clearance decision, or any override of a shop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-work-record` -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task/processing-schedule\n  scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a contamination-risk/hygiene-\n  compliance/equipment-condition concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER\n  auto-commit eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- raw-milk/dairy-materials procurement\n  proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\nprocessing-execution decision, a pasteurization-clearance decision, a\nfood-safety-clearance decision, or a shop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-pasteurization-clearance` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names six\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`dairycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-pasteurization-clearance`,\n`:declare-batch-pasteurized-and-cleared`,\n`:finalize-food-safety-clearance`, `:declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`dairycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pasteurization-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-pasteurized-and-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Maker unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered dairy products maker record\n   (`:no-maker`). Never trusts the proposal's own claim of who the\n   maker is.\n2. **Shop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an independently\n   registered dairy-processing shop site (`:no-shop`). Together with\n   check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that a\n   worker/dairy-facility record must be independently verified/\n   registered before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for declaring a batch\n   pasteurized and cleared, finalizing a food-safety clearance, or\n   overriding a shop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD,\n   PERMANENT block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated\n   unconditionally on content -- defense-in-depth on top of the\n   allowlist check: even if a future change somehow widened the\n   allowlist, content-based rejection still independently blocks\n   pasteurization/food-safety-clearance/safety-override language\n   wherever it appears in free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a contamination-risk/\n  hygiene-compliance/equipment-condition observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing about\n  food safety.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  raw-milk/dairy-materials order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  pasteurization-clearance/food-safety-clearance/safety-officer-\n  override attempt, which is why it is handled by a different\n  mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"milk\", \"pasteurization\", \"safety\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a dairy coordination actor working\nadjacent to pasteurization/food-safety work necessarily discusses\nthose concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could trigger if\nphrased carelessly. `dairycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases` is\nphrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"declare\nthe batch pasteurized and cleared\", \"finalize the food-safety\nclearance\", \"override the shop safety officer's judgment\" -- matching\nthe task's own worked example phrasing), never bare nouns, and\n`dairycoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\nwork record for maker ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\npasteurization-batch task ...\", \"... routed for shop safety officer\nreview\") WITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action\nphrases, so the regression test is a genuine stress test of the\nbare-noun-vs-action-phrase distinction, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`dairycoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercises the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7513\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7513` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7513`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 22 tests, 47 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-batch-release` that is merely\n  gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a\n  pasteurization-clearance or food-safety-clearance decision exists in\n  the code path and is merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision\n  this severe (contamination/pathogen risk, e.g. listeria), the\n  capability itself must not exist. The only op related to safety\n  escalation is `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for\n  human/shop-safety-officer attention and never itself decides,\n  authorizes, or defers a pasteurization/food-safety-clearance\n  decision for later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold raw-milk/dairy-\n  materials order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a soft\n  escalate gate, not a hard block; only the pasteurization-clearance/\n  food-safety-clearance/safety-officer-override class is a hard,\n  unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"milk\" \"pasteurization\"\n  \"safety\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses milk/\n  pasteurization/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging\n  job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale\n  text that deliberately contains those bare nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"shop safety officer\" only (vs.\n  inventing an unspecified second authority role, e.g. a separate\n  \"quality manager\"): the task's domain design names only \"a shop\n  safety officer's judgment\" as the authority figure for this\n  vertical, so a single `:override-shop-safety-officer-judgment` op\n  (plus a generic `:override-safety-officer-judgment` alias and\n  matching phrase variants) fully covers the specified scope without\n  inventing an unspecified second authority role.\n- Merging `maker` and `shop` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity provenance shape\n  (independently-registered maker AND independently-registered shop)\n  matches the CRITICAL invariant that a \"worker/dairy-facility record\n  must be independently verified/registered before any action\" and\n  the established pattern from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors\n  with two-sided provenance checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-work-record`** -- batch/inventory/progress data logging\n   only. Requires an independently registered maker AND shop\n   (`:no-maker`/`:no-shop`). Not a processing-execution,\n   pasteurization-clearance or food-safety-clearance decision in any\n   respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task/processing-schedule\n   scheduling proposal only. Cannot carry a processing-execution or\n   pasteurization-clearance decision (structurally absent from the\n   op's field shape; any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about a specific batch's\n   food-safety status -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a contamination-risk/\n   hygiene-compliance/equipment-condition concern to a human/shop\n   safety officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which a safety observation may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the shop safety officer reviews and acts entirely on their own\n   authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- raw-milk/dairy-materials\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a processing-execution,\n   pasteurization-clearance, or food-safety-clearance decision of any\n   kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action, gated by ordinary\n   cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na processing-execution decision, a pasteurization-clearance decision, a\nfood-safety-clearance decision (declaring a batch fit for sale), or a\nshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these categories are\nstructurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op\nallowlist itself (`dairycoord.governor/allowed-ops`), (b) six\nconcretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the governor-unit\nlevel (`dairycoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`dairycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-pasteurization-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-pasteurized-and-cleared`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-food-safety-clearance`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-declare-batch-fit-for-sale`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-shop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`dairycoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to declare a batch pasteurized and cleared or override a\nshop safety officer's judgment even via an otherwise-allowlisted op\n(`dairycoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-shop-safety-officer`).\n", :adr/date "2026-07-18", :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}", :test/counts "{:total 22, :assertions 47, :failures 0, :errors 0}", :actor/coordination? true, :actor/name "Dairy Shop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice", :db/id -1, :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :maker-verification :shop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation], :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7513", :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7513", :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7513], :test/simulator :dairycoord.actor-test, :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7513 — Dairy Products Makers Dairy-Shop Scheduling/Logistics Coordination Coverage", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/references [2607121000], :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7513}]
